<title>USA: Nebraska City 585 MW coal-fired unit seen back Fri.</title>
<headline>Nebraska City 585 MW coal-fired unit seen back Fri.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 585 megawatt (MW) coal-fired plant in Nebraska City, Neb., was expected to resume operation early Friday, the operator said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The plant in southeastern Nebraska near the city of Omaha was shut December 6 for chemical cleaning inside the boiler.</p>
<p>Omaha Public Power District owns and operates the Nebraska City facility.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
